Z||000002||Raydar||04-26-2000||10:30 AM||||Ross,<P>The "CJB" will be in alphabetical order with all of the other three-character RPO codes on the sticker. <BR>(There should be a couple dozen, I think.)    <BR>If the car is not in the registry, it doesn't necessarily mean it's not original. My Formula wasn't in there either. A note to Ray Paulk resulted in a copy of the original "ship-through" order, and a bunch of other info. If you need his e-mail or a link, let me know. I'll have to look, when I get home.||||reg||1
Z||000003||RossT||04-26-2000||10:42 AM||||Thank Raydar, but I have allready e-mailed Ray. He said that the vin# is not in his database, but there are still nine factory authorized t-tops out there that are not on his list. Hopefully I will be like you and get lucky. I just emailed the owner to have him check for the "cjb" code.  Cross your finger...  The dealership that sold the car was so close to C&C in Brighton, that it is most likely they took the car off the lot and had them installed aftermarket. I will still most likely buy the car.  White, tan, gold wheels, 5-speed, sub-eqradio, lumbar, and cloth. 18000 miles. Prey for CJB.<P>thanks for you input.<P>Ross||||reg||1
